  "java_adaptations": [
    "Common six-button pause layout retained with Java achievements; Leaderboards opens native local statistics.",
    "Host Options remains accessible through Square or H in the pause menu.",
    "Reset to Defaults confirms and resets the console profile; native Java settings retain their existing values.",
    "At the user's request, settings match Help & Options: 225x20 buttons on a 25-pixel pitch, with scrolling instead of smaller controls (up to eight rows at 4x and five at Auto on 1440p).",
    "The four implemented Help & Options actions follow their source order; console-only reinstall/debug services are not added.",
    "Menu prompts use the original 5% HD left safe-zone margin; existing in-game hints retain their separate placement.",
    "Pause and Host Options now use the same user-requested Help & Options geometry; compact pause viewports scroll instead of reducing button dimensions.",
    "Player-inventory selection fills the original holder interior behind item sprites; exclusive full-holder hit bounds keep touching slots singly selected.",
    "Contiguous Load/Create/Join rows share the original single-pixel outer edge; only the following row owns mouse hits on the seam."
  ]
